the manner in which the approval of the owners of rights regarding collection and distribution of fees, approval for
utilisation of any amount collected as fees and to provide to such owners information concerning activities in relation to
the administration of their rights under sub-section (1) of section 35;
(cg)
the returns to be filed by copyright societies to the Registrar of Copyrights under sub-section (1) of section 36;
(d)
the manners of determining any royalties payable under this Act, and the security to be taken for the payment of such
royalties;
(da)
the manner of payment of royalty under clause (j) of sub-section (1) of section 52;
(e)
the form of Register of Copyrights to be kept under this Act and the particulars to be entered therein;
(f)
the matters in respect of which the Registrar of Copyrights and the Copyright Board shall have powers of a civil court;
(g)
the fees which may be payable under this Act;
(h)
the regulation of business of the Copyright Office and of all things by this Act placed under the direction or control of the
Registrar of Copyrights.
